WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:01.830
A bit of a peek behind the curtain as to what's
been going on.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:07.290
A great look into the chaos that is taking
place behind the scenes at the white house

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:13.070
came to us yesterday in the form of a vanity
fair article by Gabriel Sherman.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:18.650
And one interesting little tidbit is that
Donald Trump has pulled Rudy Giuliani off

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:23.500
of Fox news appearances again because they
are so disastrous.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.199
This actually is not the first time that this
has happened.

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:31.650
You might remember back in March, we did a
story called what happened to Rudy Giuliani

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.730
because we noticed that after some embarrassing
television appearances by Rudy, he suddenly

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.370
just wasn't being interviewed anywhere period.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.250
And this lasted for some month.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.210
Eventually Rudy resurfaced, but it is now
happening again.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:49.210
Now, the public facing funny part is there's
old Rudy making a FA, uh, making a fool of

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.400
himself on television, yet again all the time
he's contradicting himself.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.190
He's self incriminating.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.230
He's admitting to things that Trump is still
publicly denying.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.570
We've got to get Rudy off of TV.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:04.870
But then there's the more sort of serious
behind the scenes piece, which is predictable,

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.030
which is that people around Donald Trump,
including Jared Cushner, his son in law, and

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:14.460
Ivanka Trump, his daughter have been telling
Trump, you've got to fire Rudy for the better

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.240
part of a year according to this report in
vanity fair by Gabriel Sherman.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.730
Now, of course, Trump has not fired Rudy,
but there have been questions as to is Rudy

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.750
still Trump's lawyer or not?

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.770
But there's more and more speculation that
Rudy Giuliani could end up arrested over.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:35.370
The Ukraine fiasco is two of his associates
already have, Trump has stood by Rudy so far,

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:40.400
but the pressure has mounted more and more
and now Donald Trump has at least in the immediate

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.670
told Rudy Giuliani, no more Fox news appearances
for you.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:50.020
This has been corroborated seemingly anyway,
circumstantially by Fox news producers who

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.061
said to vanity fair, you know, in the last
few days we actually did invite Rudy Giuliani

00:01:54.061 --> 00:01:56.270
to appear and he turned us down.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.050
So it seems as though this is indeed what's
going on.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:04.299
One Republican is quoted by Gabriel Sherman
in this article as saying, quote Rudy is cut

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:06.200
off from Fox news.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:13.730
Now there's a second layer of funny, and when
you look at what was the last straw or the

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:19.380
straw that broke the camel's back on this,
it is something really, really funny at every

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.380
appearance.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:25.730
Rudy has been a pathetic joke, but what pushed
Trump over the edge is reportedly when Rudy

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:31.380
went on TV on November 23rd and said, I have
an insurance policy against Trump in case

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.960
he turns on me, that did not go over well.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.590
Rudy later tweeted that the, that the comment
was a joke.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:40.700
It was sarcastic.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.180
It wasn't for real, but Trump didn't like
it.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.540
And at that point said no more Fox news for
Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:54.080
So as usual with Trump, it's, yes, of course
have Rudy do interviews was always a bad idea.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.770
Your TV lawyer can't seem to help but further
incriminate himself and you.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:04.959
But then the acute reason that actually got
Rudy pulled off is less about incriminating

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:08.840
Trump, but merely saying something that was
supposedly a joke that Trump didn't like,

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.800
which is, Oh, if Trump turns on me, I've got
an insurance policy against him.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.980
It's a never ending comedy of errors.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.270
It's a race to the bottom, so to speak, in
political discourse.

